Prompt: '<|im_start|>user\nlist all prime numbers within 100<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n'
Completion: "<think>\nOkay, so I need to list all the prime numbers between 100. Let me think. First, I remember that a prime number is a number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself. So, starting from 100, I need to check each number to see if it's prime.\n\nLet me start counting from 100 upwards. The first prime number after 100 is 101. Wait, is 101 a prime number? Let me verify. To check if 101 is prime, I can try dividing it by numbers less than its square root. The square root of 101 is approximately 10.05, so I only need to check primes up to 10. The primes up to 10 are 2, 3, 5, 7. 101 divided by 2 is 50.5, so not divisible. Divided by 3, 101/3 is around 33.666..., not an integer. Divided by 5, ends with 1, so no. Divided by 7, 101"
